    <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="Package1" name="DataTypes">
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" xmi:id="PrimitiveType1" name="AnyURI">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment45" annotatedElement="PrimitiveType1">
          <body>A Uniform Resource Identifier (URI). The value space of AnyURI is the same as that of the XML Schema data type anyURI [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#anyURI] as specified by the W3C Recommendation XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2] from October 28, 2004.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" xmi:id="PrimitiveType2" name="Boolean">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment46" annotatedElement="PrimitiveType2">
          <body>One of the boolean values true or false. The value space of Boolean is the same as that of the XML Schema data type boolean [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#boolean] as specified by the W3C Recommendation XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2] from October 28, 2004.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" xmi:id="PrimitiveType3" name="DateTime">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment47" annotatedElement="PrimitiveType3">
          <body>A date time. The value space of DateTime is the same as that of the XML Schema data type dateTime [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#dateTime] as specified by the W3C Recommendation XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2] from October 28, 2004, with the exception that DateTime values do not carry any timezone information.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" xmi:id="PrimitiveType4" name="Double">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment48" annotatedElement="PrimitiveType4">
          <body>A double-precision 64-bit floating point number. The value space of Double is the same as that of the XML Schema data type double [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double] as specified by the W3C Recommendation XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2] from October 28, 2004, with the exception that the special values positive infinity (INF), negative infinity (-INF), and not-a-number (NaN) are excluded from the value space of Double.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" xmi:id="PrimitiveType5" name="Integer">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment49" annotatedElement="PrimitiveType5">
          <body>An integer number. The value space of Integer is the same as that of the XML Schema data type integer [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer] as specified by the W3C Recommendation XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2] from October 28, 2004.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType9" name="MultiLanguageString">
        <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="Property27" name="SingleLanguageStrings" type="DataType21">
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment50" annotatedElement="Property27">
            <body>The SingleLanguageStrings with language-dependent values for the MultiLanguageString.</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="LiteralUnlimitedNatural1" value="*"/>
        </ownedAttribute>
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment51" annotatedElement="DataType9">
          <body>A container for one or more SingleLanguageStrings. MultiLanguageString is used as the type of data attributes which have language-dependent string values: Each SingleLanguageString contains a NullableString Value and a Language tag.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:InstanceSpecification" xmi:id="InstanceSpecification0" classifier="DataType22" name="NULL_ANY_URI"/>
