        <generalization xmi:type="uml:Generalization" xmi:id="Generalization20" general="DataType1"/>
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment52" annotatedElement="DataType22">
          <body>A null value for a value of type NullableAnyURI. The only instance of this singleton type is NULL_ANY_URI.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType23" name="NullDateTime">
        <generalization xmi:type="uml:Generalization" xmi:id="Generalization21" general="DataType26"/>
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment53" annotatedElement="DataType23">
          <body>A null value for a value of type NullableDateTime. The only instance of this singleton type is NULL_DATE_TIME.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType24" name="NullInteger">
        <generalization xmi:type="uml:Generalization" xmi:id="Generalization22" general="DataType5"/>
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment54" annotatedElement="DataType24">
          <body>A null value for a value of type NullableInteger. The only instance of this singleton type is NULL_INTEGER.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType25" name="NullString">
        <generalization xmi:type="uml:Generalization" xmi:id="Generalization23" general="DataType16"/>
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment55" annotatedElement="DataType25">
          <body>A null value for a value of type NullableString. The only instance of this singleton type is NULL_STRING.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType1" isAbstract="true" name="NullableAnyURI">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment56" annotatedElement="DataType1">
          <body>A Uniform Resource Identifier (URI), or a null value. NullableAnyURI is abstract and has two concrete subtypes:
- an AnyURI is an actual value for a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI);
- a NullAnyURI is a null value that explicitly indicates the absence of a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI).</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType26" isAbstract="true" name="NullableDateTime">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment57" annotatedElement="DataType26">
          <body>A date time, or a null value. NullableDateTime is abstract and has two concrete subtypes:
- a DateTime is an actual value for a date time;
- a NullDateTime is a null value that explicitly indicates the absence of a date time.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType5" isAbstract="true" name="NullableInteger">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment58" annotatedElement="DataType5">
          <body>An integer number, or a null value. NullableInteger is abstract and has two concrete subtypes:
- an Integer is an actual value for an integer number;
- a NullInteger is a null value that explicitly indicates the absence of an integer number.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType16" isAbstract="true" name="NullableString">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment59" annotatedElement="DataType16">
          <body>A sequence of characters, or a null value. NullableString is abstract and has two concrete subtypes:
- a String is an actual value for a sequence of characters;
- a NullString is a null value that explicitly indicates the absence of a sequence of characters.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:DataType" xmi:id="DataType21" name="SingleLanguageString">
        <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="Property28" name="Language" type="DataType16">
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment60" annotatedElement="Property28">
            <body>The language of the Value of the SingleLanguageString. If not NULL_STRING, the language must be given as a language tag standardized by IETF BCP 47 (Best Current Practice 47 by the Internet Engineering Task Force). IETF BCP 47 is based on ISO 639.
In DEXPI, only those language tags are allowed
- that are listed in the normative registry file at https://www.iana.org/assignments/language-subtag-registry/language-subtag-registry [https://www.iana.org/assignments/language-subtag-registry/language-subtag-registry] from September 29, 2020,
- that consist of exactly two letters (in particular extended tags such as en-US or de-CH-1996 are not allowed),
- that refer to an actual language (the type defined by IETF BCP 47 must be language),
- and that are not deprecated.
The table below contains all permitted language tags.
[TABLE SKIPPED IN EXCEL EXPORT; SEE PDF OR HTML]</body>
          </ownedComment>
        </ownedAttribute>
        <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="Property29" name="Value" type="DataType16">
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment61" annotatedElement="Property29">
            <body>The actual NullableString value of the SingleLanguageString.</body>
          </ownedComment>
        </ownedAttribute>
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment62" annotatedElement="DataType21">
          <body>A SingleLanguageString contains a NullableString as its Value and a Language tag. SingleLanguageString is only used within MultiLanguageString. See the latter data type for more details.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" xmi:id="PrimitiveType0" name="String">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment63" annotatedElement="PrimitiveType0">
          <body>A sequence of characters. The value space of String is the same as that of the XML Schema data type string [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string] as specified by the W3C Recommendation XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2] from October 28, 2004.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" xmi:id="PrimitiveType6" name="UnsignedByte">
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="Comment64" annotatedElement="PrimitiveType6">
          <body>An integer number in the range from 0 to 255 (inclusively). The value space of UnsignedByte is the same as that of the XML Schema data type unsignedByte [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#unsignedByte] as specified by the W3C Recommendation XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition [https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2] from October 28, 2004.</body>
        </ownedComment>
      </packagedElement>
    </packagedElement>
